Yii 1.1.x CPgsqlSchema::findConstraints unions pg_constraint.contype ("char") with
text literals, which PostgreSQL >= 10 rejects with
  ERROR:  UNION types "char" and text cannot be matched
so every table's metadata lookup fails and the api returns a CDbException.
Casting both sides to text keeps the query identical in meaning.

--- a/framework/db/schema/pgsql/CPgsqlSchema.php	2020-12-02 16:53:51.000000000 +0000
+++ b/framework/db/schema/pgsql/CPgsqlSchema.php	2026-08-30 11:32:06.951722172 +0000
@@ -239,7 +239,7 @@
 	SELECT
 		conname,
 		pg_catalog.pg_get_constraintdef(oid) AS consrc,
-		contype,
+		contype::text AS contype,
 		conrelid AS relid,
 		NULL AS indkey
 	FROM
@@ -251,9 +251,9 @@
 		pc.relname,
 		NULL,
 		CASE WHEN indisprimary THEN
-				'p'
+				'p'::text
 		ELSE
-				'u'
+				'u'::text
 		END,
 		pi.indrelid,
 		indkey
